# Local env files must never ship — Vercel injects env vars from the dashboard.
# (vercel deploy uploads the working dir and does NOT honor .gitignore, so a
# leaked .env AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000 was overriding the real host and
# breaking the /admin auth cookie. Keep these out of the deployment.)
.env
.env.local
.env.development
.env.development.local
.env.production.local
.env*.local

# Photo working folders. Production deploys come from GitHub, which already
# honours .gitignore — but `vercel deploy` from the CLI uploads the working
# directory and does not, so without these it would push ~240 MB of raw
# camera originals. Nothing in the site references either folder.
/public/images/originals/
/public/images/thumbs/
